     "Hello,<div><br></div><div>I am wondering what is the best way to use gheatmap in order to get a figure like this <a href=\"https://yulab-smu.top/treedata-book/treedata_files/figure-html/gheatmap-1.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://yulab-smu.top/treedata-book/treedata_files/figure-html/gheatmap-1.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481718128000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3RSvoKu5Heb-9Df-3gdIYj\">https://yulab-smu.top/treedata-book/treedata_files/figure-html/gheatmap-1.png</a> (Panel A) without getting the x axis labels trimmed. I&#39;ve really digged in a lot of questions on the web but couldn&#39;t find any clue.</div><div><br></div><div>Any suggestion is much appreciated!</div>"
