     1,
     "<div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">I think you can increase the lower limit of <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">y</code> by adding <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">scale_y_continuous(limits = c(-1, NA))</code>.</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">&gt; library(ggtree)\r\nBioconductor version 3.12 (BiocManager 1.30.12), ?BiocManager::install for help\r\nggtree v2.4.2  For help: <a href=\"https://yulab-smu.top/treedata-book/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://yulab-smu.top/treedata-book/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481718130000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3oRytWt6HmUfhfeo7dq1Mx\">https://yulab-smu.top/treedata-book/</a>\r\n\r\nIf you use ggtree in published research, please cite the most appropriate paper(s):\r\n\r\n1. Guangchuang Yu. Using ggtree to visualize data on tree-like structures. Current Protocols in Bioinformatics, 2020, 69:e96. doi:10.1002/cpbi.96\r\n2. Guangchuang Yu, Tommy Tsan-Yuk Lam, Huachen Zhu, Yi Guan. Two methods for mapping and visualizing associated data on phylogeny using ggtree. Molecular Biology and Evolution 2018, 35(12):3041-3043. doi:10.1093\r\n/molbev/msy194\r\n3. Guangchuang Yu, David Smith, Huachen Zhu, Yi Guan, Tommy Tsan-Yuk Lam. ggtree: an R package for visualization and annotation of phylogenetic trees with their covariates and other associated data. Methods in E\r\ncology and Evolution 2017, 8(1):28-36. doi:10.1111/2041-210X.12628\r\n\r\n&gt; library(treeio)\r\ntreeio v1.15.7  For help: <a href=\"https://yulab-smu.top/treedata-book/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://yulab-smu.top/treedata-book/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792481718130000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3oRytWt6HmUfhfeo7dq1Mx\">https://yulab-smu.top/treedata-book/</a>\r\n\r\nIf you use treeio in published research, please cite:\r\n\r\nLG Wang, TTY Lam, S Xu, Z Dai, L Zhou, T Feng, P Guo, CW Dunn, BR Jones, T Bradley, H Zhu, Y Guan, Y Jiang, G Yu. treeio: an R package for phylogenetic tree input and output with richly annotated and associated \r\ndata. Molecular Biology and Evolution 2020, 37(2):599-603. doi: 10.1093/molbev/msz240\r\n\r\n&gt; beast_file &lt;- system.file(&quot;examples/MCC_FluA_H3.tree&quot;, package=&quot;ggtree&quot;)\r\n&gt; beast_tree &lt;- read.beast(beast_file)\r\n&gt;\r\n&gt; genotype_file &lt;- system.file(&quot;examples/Genotype.txt&quot;, package=&quot;ggtree&quot;)\r\n&gt; genotype &lt;- read.table(genotype_file, sep=&quot;\\t&quot;, stringsAsFactor=F)\r\n&gt; colnames(genotype) &lt;- sub(&quot;\\\\.$&quot;, &quot;&quot;, colnames(genotype))\r\n&gt; p &lt;- ggtree(beast_tree, mrsd=&quot;2013-01-01&quot;) +\r\n      geom_treescale(x=2008, y=1, offset=2) +\r\n      geom_tiplab(size=2)\r\n&gt; p\r\n&gt; p1 &lt;- gheatmap(p, genotype, offset=5, width=0.5, font.size=3,\r\n          colnames_angle=-45, hjust=0) +\r\n      scale_fill_manual(breaks=c(&quot;HuH3N2&quot;, &quot;pdm&quot;, &quot;trig&quot;),\r\n          values=c(&quot;steelblue&quot;, &quot;firebrick&quot;, &quot;darkgreen&quot;), name=&quot;genotype&quot;)\r\n\r\n&gt; p1 + ggplot2::scale_y_continuous(limit=c(-1, NA))\r\n</code></pre><div title=\"MDH:PGRpdj5JIHRoaW5rIHlvdSBjYW4gaW5jcmVhc2UgdGhlIGxvd2VyIGxpbWl0IG9mIGB5YCBieSBh\r\nZGRpbmcgYHNjYWxlX3lfY29udGludW91cyhsaW1pdHMgPSBjKC0xLCBOQSkpYC48YnI+PC9kaXY+\r\nPGRpdj48YnI+PC9kaXY+YGBgPGRpdj48ZGl2PiZndDsgbGlicmFyeShnZ3RyZWUpPC9kaXY+PGRp\r\ndj5CaW9jb25kdWN0b3IgdmVyc2lvbiAzLjEyIChCaW9jTWFuYWdlciAxLjMwLjEyKSwgP0Jpb2NN\r\nYW5hZ2VyOjppbnN0YWxsIGZvciBoZWxwPC9kaXY+PGRpdj5nZ3RyZWUgdjIuNC4yJm5ic3A7IEZv\r\nciBoZWxwOiBodHRwczovL3l1bGFiLXNtdS50b3AvdHJlZWRhdGEtYm9vay88L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pjxi\r\ncj48L2Rpdj48ZGl2PklmIHlvdSB1c2UgZ2d0cmVlIGluIHB1Ymxpc2hlZCByZXNlYXJjaCwgcGxl\r\nYXNlIGNpdGUgdGhlIG1vc3QgYXBwcm9wcmlhdGUgcGFwZXIocyk6PC9kaXY+PGRpdj48YnI+PC9k\r\naXY+PGRpdj4xLiBHdWFuZ2NodWFuZyBZdS4gVXNpbmcgZ2d0cmVlIHRvIHZpc3VhbGl6ZSBkYXRh\r\nIG9uIHRyZWUtbGlrZSBzdHJ1Y3R1cmVzLiBDdXJyZW50IFByb3RvY29scyBpbiBCaW9pbmZvcm1h\r\ndGljcywgMjAyMCwgNjk6ZTk2LiBkb2k6MTAuMTAwMi9jcGJpLjk2PC9kaXY+PGRpdj4yLiBHdWFu\r\nZ2NodWFuZyBZdSwgVG9tbXkgVHNhbi1ZdWsgTGFtLCBIdWFjaGVuIFpodSwgWWkgR3Vhbi4gVHdv\r\nIG1ldGhvZHMgZm9yIG1hcHBpbmcgYW5kIHZpc3VhbGl6aW5nIGFzc29jaWF0ZWQgZGF0YSBvbiBw\r\naHlsb2dlbnkgdXNpbmcgZ2d0cmVlLiBNb2xlY3VsYXIgQmlvbG9neSBhbmQgRXZvbHV0aW9uIDIw\r\nMTgsIDM1KDEyKTozMDQxLTMwNDMuIGRvaToxMC4xMDkzPC9kaXY+PGRpdj4vbW9sYmV2L21zeTE5\r\nNDwvZGl2PjxkaXY+My4gR3VhbmdjaHVhbmcgWXUsIERhdmlkIFNtaXRoLCBIdWFjaGVuIFpodSwg\r\nWWkgR3VhbiwgVG9tbXkgVHNhbi1ZdWsgTGFtLiBnZ3RyZWU6IGFuIFIgcGFja2FnZSBmb3Igdmlz\r\ndWFsaXphdGlvbiBhbmQgYW5ub3RhdGlvbiBvZiBwaHlsb2dlbmV0aWMgdHJlZXMgd2l0aCB0aGVp\r\nciBjb3ZhcmlhdGVzIGFuZCBvdGhlciBhc3NvY2lhdGVkIGRhdGEuIE1ldGhvZHMgaW4gRTwvZGl2\r\nPjxkaXY+Y29sb2d5IGFuZCBFdm9sdXRpb24gMjAxNywgOCgxKToyOC0zNi4gZG9pOjEwLjExMTEv\r\nMjA0MS0yMTBYLjEyNjI4PC9kaXY+PGRpdj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj4mZ3Q7IGxpYnJhcnkodHJl\r\nZWlvKTwvZGl2PjxkaXY+dHJlZWlvIHYxLjE1LjcmbmJzcDsgRm9yIGhlbHA6IGh0dHBzOi8veXVs\r\nYWItc211LnRvcC90cmVlZGF0YS1ib29rLzwvZGl2PjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+SWYgeW91\r\nIHVzZSB0cmVlaW8gaW4gcHVibGlzaGVkIHJlc2VhcmNo